<title>USA: All-American FY 1996 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>All-American FY 1996 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>ALL AMERICAN SEMICONDUCTOR, INC.</p>
<p>CONSOLIDATED CONDENSED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>(Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p> Years Ended December 31		     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net Sales (1)			   $   237,846    $   177,335</p>
<p> Income from Continuing Operations (2)   2,804	    6,925</p>
<p>Income (Loss) from Continuing Operations</p>
<p>Before Discontinued Operations and Extraordinary</p>
<p>     Items (3)				 (1,691)	    2,450</p>
<p> Discontinued Operations		   (1,757)		 79</p>
<p> Extraordinary Items				58		  -</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) (3)		     (3,390)	    2,529</p>
<p> Earnings (Loss) Per Share (3)	     (.17)		.16</p>
<p>Average Number of Common</p>
<p>    Shares Outstanding		  20,115,843     15,945,696</p>
<p>NOTES: Net sales figures do not include $6.8 million in 1996 and $3.5 million in 1995, of discontinued operations.</p>
<p>Income from discontinued operations do not give effect to an inventory write-off of $2 million in 1996 and restructuring and other nonrecurring expenses of $4.9 million in 1996 and $1.1 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Income (loss) from continued operations before discontinued operations do not give effect to the after-tax effects of the inventory write-off and restructuring and other nonrecurring expenses and a write-off of deferred financing fees of $1.1 million, on an after-tax basis, in 1996.  After giving effect to the foregoing the company recognized a net loss of $9.9 million, or $.49 per share for 1996 and $1.9 million, or $.12 per share for 1995.</p>
